---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ifric/ifric5.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Two Separate Items, Not One Net Balance" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Accounting for the Fund Interest" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Reimbursement Rights vs Consolidation" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Obligations to Make Additional Contributions" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Rights to Surplus Distributions" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Changes in the Carrying Amount of the Interest" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "IFRIC 5 vs US GAAP" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Why offsetting the wrong way would mislead</div>
        <div class="principle">Contributors to decommissioning funds often assume their obligation and their fund interest are simply two sides of the same coin and could be presented net. IFRIC 5 exists because that intuition conflicts with IAS 1's general prohibition on offsetting assets and liabilities — the contributor's obligation to a THIRD PARTY (the ultimate site owner/regulator) and its INTEREST in a separately-managed fund are, in substance, distinct rights and obligations against different counterparties.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Faithful representation of a restricted asset</div>
        <div class="principle">A contributor typically cannot access fund assets freely — access is restricted to reimbursement of decommissioning expenditure. Recognising the fund interest as an unrestricted asset, or netting it against the liability, would obscure that restriction from users of the financial statements. IFRIC 5's gross presentation preserves that information.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope & Definitions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What IFRIC 5 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 5 applies to a contributor's accounting for interests arising from decommissioning funds that have BOTH of these characteristics: (a) the fund's assets are administered separately from the contributor's own assets, and (b) the contributor's access to fund assets is restricted.</div>
        <div class="elabel">TYPICAL FACT PATTERNS</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>Nuclear decommissioning trust funds</span>
          <span>Mine rehabilitation funds jointly funded by multiple operators</span>
          <span>Environmental remediation funds administered by an independent trustee</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Fund</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Assets segregated in a separate, restricted vehicle to fund some or all of the costs of decommissioning, restoring, or rehabilitating an asset or site.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Contributor</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">An entity that makes contributions to a fund, separately from its own recognised decommissioning obligation under IAS 37.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Two Separate Items, Not One Net Balance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">The central mechanic</div>
        <div class="principle">A contributor recognises TWO separate items: (1) its OBLIGATION to pay decommissioning costs as a liability under IAS 37, and (2) its INTEREST in the fund, recognised separately UNLESS the contributor is required to make good any shortfall in the fund, in which case a right of reimbursement may instead be recognised under IAS 37's own reimbursement provisions.</div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--flush">⚠️ The two items are NOT offset against one another on the statement of financial position — IFRIC 5 requires gross presentation, consistent with IAS 1's general offsetting prohibition.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Accounting for the Fund Interest</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The default treatment</div>
        <div class="principle">Where the contributor's right to receive reimbursement from the fund is NOT unconditional, the interest is recognised as a reimbursement right under IAS 37, measured at the LOWER of: (a) the amount of the related decommissioning obligation, and (b) the contributor's share of the fair value of the net assets of the fund attributable to contributors.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Worked example — reimbursement right measurement</div>
        <div class="worked">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Applying the lower-of test</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A contributor's share of the decommissioning obligation is $5,000,000. Its share of the fair value of the fund's net assets is $4,200,000.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The reimbursement right is recognised at $4,200,000 — the LOWER of the two amounts. The full $5,000,000 obligation remains recognised gross as a liability; the $800,000 shortfall is not reduced by any asset recognition.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Reimbursement Rights vs Consolidation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">When the fund itself must be consolidated or equity accounted</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">IFRIC 5's reimbursement-right mechanics apply only where the contributor does NOT control, jointly control, or have significant influence over the fund. Where the contributor DOES have such a relationship with the fund, it instead accounts for its interest under IFRS 10 (consolidation), IFRS 11 (joint arrangements), or IAS 28 (associates), as applicable.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Obligations to Make Additional Contributions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">A separate liability, recognised on its own terms</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Where a contributor has an obligation to make potential additional contributions — for example, if other contributors default, or the fund's assets prove insufficient — that obligation is recognised as a SEPARATE liability, assessed under IAS 37's own recognition criteria, independently of the reimbursement right.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Rights to Surplus Distributions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">A high recognition threshold</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A contributor's right to a refund of any surplus from the fund — after all decommissioning obligations are settled — is recognised as an ASSET only if the surplus is VIRTUALLY CERTAIN to be available to the contributor. This deliberately sets a much higher bar than the "probable" threshold used elsewhere in IAS 37.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Changes in the Carrying Amount of the Interest</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Where subsequent movements are recognised</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Changes in the carrying amount of the reimbursement right — OTHER than contributions paid into the fund and payments received or receivable from the fund for decommissioning costs incurred — are recognised in profit or loss in the period they occur. This captures, for example, changes in the fair value of the fund's net assets that affect the lower-of measurement outcome.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What IFRIC 5 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Nature of the contributor's interest in a fund, and any restrictions on access to fund assets</span>
          <span>Nature and amount of any obligation to make potential additional contributions</span>
          <span>Fair value of assets held by the fund, to the extent the interest is measured at the contributor's share of that fair value</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Whether the contributor has control, joint control, or significant influence over the fund</span>
              <span>Whether a surplus refund right meets the "virtually certain" threshold</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Fair value of the contributor's share of the fund's net assets at each reporting date</span>
              <span>Likelihood and amount of potential additional contribution obligations</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>IFRIC 5 vs US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — IFRIC 5 vs US GAAP</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IFRIC 5 (IFRS)</span><span>US GAAP</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Measurement of the fund interest</span><span>Lower of the obligation and the contributor's share of the fund's net asset fair value</span><span>Generally values the trust interest at fair value directly</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Surplus refund recognition threshold</span><span>Virtually certain — a high bar</span><span>No single codified "virtually certain" threshold</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Presentation</span><span>Gross — obligation and interest presented separately</span><span>Generally also gross</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Gross presentation is a shared principle across both frameworks; the more consequential divergence is in how the contributor's INTEREST in the fund is measured and capped.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every IFRIC 5 event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Recognition of the decommissioning obligation</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Under IAS 37, gross</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Recognition of the reimbursement right</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Separate asset, at the lower of the two measurement bases</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Contribution paid into the fund</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Increases the carrying amount of the interest</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Change in carrying amount other than contributions or payments</span><span><span class="badge bp">SOPL</span></span><span>Recognised in the period it occurs</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Additional contribution obligation</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Separate IAS 37 liability</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IAS 37</span><span>Governs the underlying decommissioning obligation and reimbursement-right mechanics</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 10 / IFRS 11 / IAS 28</span><span>Apply instead of the reimbursement-right approach where the contributor controls or significantly influences the fund</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IFRIC 1</span><span>Governs how changes in the related decommissioning liability itself are accounted for</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>IAS 1</span><span>Supplies the general offsetting prohibition underlying IFRIC 5's gross presentation requirement</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Reimbursement right</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">An asset recognised under IAS 37 when a third party is expected to reimburse some or all of the expenditure required to settle a provision — capped so as not to exceed the amount of the related provision.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Virtually certain</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A very high probability threshold, well above "probable," used sparingly across IFRS — here applied to a contributor's right to a residual fund surplus.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Reimbursement right", definition: "An asset recognised under IAS 37 when a third party is expected to reimburse some or all of the expenditure required to settle a provision." },
      { term: "Virtually certain", definition: "A very high probability threshold, well above 'probable,' used sparingly across IFRS." },
      { term: "Restricted assets", definition: "Fund assets to which the contributor's access is limited, typically to reimbursement of qualifying decommissioning expenditure." }
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.IFRIC5} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
